---
import VisionFigure from '../VisionFigure.astro';
import SectionHead from '../SectionHead.astro';
---

<section data-vision-section class="band-cream section">
  <SectionHead num="12 / 14 — Context" heading="Bowl country." />

  <div class="container-page">
    <VisionFigure num="11" title="The Valley as a bowl">
      <svg
        class="basin"
        viewBox="0 0 600 240"
        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Cross-section of the Las Vegas Valley basin: mountains rise on both sides; the valley floor sits between them; sun shines from above; arrows show heat and pollution trapped in the bowl."
      >
        <circle class="basin-sun" cx="540" cy="50" r="14"></circle>
        <text class="basin-axis" x="540" y="80" text-anchor="middle">Sun</text>
        <path
          class="basin-mts"
          d="M0 240 L0 160 L80 80 L150 130 L220 90 L260 160 L340 110 L380 140 L440 100 L520 150 L580 90 L600 130 L600 240 Z"
        ></path>
        <line class="basin-floor" x1="220" y1="180" x2="440" y2="180" stroke-dasharray="3 4"></line>
        <text class="basin-label" x="330" y="200" text-anchor="middle">Valley floor</text>
        <text class="basin-axis" x="80" y="170">Spring Mts</text>
        <text class="basin-axis" x="540" y="170">Sunrise · Eldorado</text>
        <path class="basin-arrow" d="M280 60 L280 130" marker-end="url(#down-arrow)"></path>
        <path class="basin-arrow" d="M310 80 L310 140"></path>
        <path class="basin-arrow" d="M250 90 L250 130"></path>
        <text class="basin-label" x="330" y="60" fill="var(--color-accent)"
          >Heat &amp; air don't leave</text
        >
        <defs>
          <marker
            id="down-arrow"
            markerWidth="10"
            markerHeight="10"
            refX="5"
            refY="9"
            orient="auto"
          >
            <path d="M0,0 L5,10 L10,0 Z" fill="var(--color-accent)"></path>
          </marker>
        </defs>
      </svg>
      <Fragment slot="caption">
        Mountains on every side mean pollutants and summer heat get trapped over the Valley floor.
        The basin doesn't move. What we put in it does.
      </Fragment>
    </VisionFigure>
  </div>

  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="vision-prose">
      <p>
        The Las&nbsp;Vegas Valley sits in a literal geographic bowl. The Spring Mountains rise to
        the west, the Sheep Range to the north, the Sunrise and Eldorado mountains to the east, the
        McCullough range to the south. On most days of most months, air settles into the bowl and
        stays there until the next weather front moves through. So does heat. So does whatever
        leaves a tailpipe.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is why air-quality alerts in the Valley aren't an occasional summer event but a routine
        summer pattern. It's why ozone exceedance days are climbing and why pediatric asthma
        diagnoses are climbing with them. It's why heat-illness call volume from bus stops without
        shade is what it is. None of this is going to change because we wish it would. The basin
        doesn't move. The mountains don't get shorter. The Mojave is what we have.
      </p>
      <p>
        What can change is what we put in the basin. A bus running on hydrogen fuel cells replaces
        the tailpipes of forty cars when it runs full. A BRT station with shade keeps a
        twelve-minute wait from being a heat-illness call. Phoenix — hotter than us, just as
        car-built — has already shown that great transit works in extreme heat, and Salt Lake has
        shown that a sprawling Western metro can build rail and fill it. The desert is not an
        excuse. It is the reason.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="vision-tail">
      A sustainable oasis in the desert. Made possible through public transportation.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .basin {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    max-height: 280px;
  }
  .basin-mts {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 14%, transparent);
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .basin-floor {
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1;
    opacity: 0.3;
  }
  .basin-arrow {
    stroke: var(--color-accent);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    fill: none;
  }
  .basin-sun {
    fill: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .basin-label {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    fill: currentColor;
  }
  .basin-axis {
    font-size: 9px;
    font-weight: 600;
    fill: var(--vp-text-muted);
  }
</style>
